  "notes": "Cash basis, governmental funds only (no business-type funds). Statement lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4). The statement prints cash basis fund balances (beginning 13,073,977, ending 13,331,522), recorded as fund balance; no beginning cash is printed (beginning_cash null); ending cash and cash equivalents 10,253,613 and investments 3,077,909 are on the p3 balance sheet (top-level cash left null since the roll-forward measure is fund balance). Statement 'Taxes: Other' 183,337 split: Visitor Promotion Fund's Other taxes 20,700 -> lodging tax (fund name), remainder 162,637 other taxes (printed Other taxes of General, Road, E911 and 911 Wireless Service funds). Balance sheet from the governmental funds Statement of Cash Basis Assets and Fund Balances (p3), whose totals equal the Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (pp5-6; Taxes 6,113,768 split with the p4 General Fund column; final budget 6,108,882 for Taxes not allocated to pieces); major funds budget schedules (pp7-8; the COVID ARPA Fund's one-line Disbursements 1,056,244 split by function from its p4 column); nonmajor funds from the combining statement by fund (pp11-12), which is more detailed than the one-line nonmajor budget schedules (pp9-10), so those are not recorded (no double counting). Funds with no activity (Road Sinking, Drug Law Enforcement and Education) have no detail lines. Noxious Weed Control (General Fund, Public Works heading) -> natural resources/conservation. Read pages 1-12 of 12"
